  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Available Data**\n\nOkay, I\'m examining the initial screen, specifically \"In\303\255cio,\" which appears to be a dashboard or home screen. I\'ve noted the \"LabReserve - In\303\255cio\" profile header, the notification bell alert, and the avatar of Prof. Andr\303\251. I am now working through the content of the image.\n\n\n**Interpreting Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the textual and visual elements. \"Ol\303\241, Prof. Andr\303\251 \360\237\221\213\" establishes the user. I have logged the department. The metrics and \"Next Class Spotlight\" card offer key insights. The card shows specific class details, along with software and location, plus access options. I\'m noting the clear call to action buttons at the bottom.\n\n\n**Examining Upcoming Reservations**\n\nI\'m now diving into the \"Programa\303\247\303\243o de Software\" section. I am observing the upcoming reservations, noting specifics like course names (\"Programa\303\247\303\243o Web III,\" \"Intelig\303\252ncia Artificial\"), lab locations, dates, times, and confirmation statuses. I\'m paying close attention to the \"Aguardando TI\" status for the AI class, specifically call #4892. I am assessing the QR code modal and its associated access code and countdown.\n\n**Detailing Reservation Steps**\n\nI\'ve transitioned to the \"Nova Reserva\" screen and am reviewing \"Passo 1: Requisitos.\" I am going through the stepper which includes, \"Requisitos,\" \"Escolha da Sala,\" and \"Confirma\303\247\303\243o.\" I am noting the discipline and class selection options, plus the student count mechanism, including the \"32 esta\303\247\303\265es ativas\" display, decrement/increment controls, the slider for fine-tuning, and the recommendation for labs. I am checking the date and time selection, and its horizontal scrollable date chips.\n\n\n**Reviewing Lab Selection**\n\nI\'m now on \"Passo 2: Escolha da Sala,\" focused on available labs after filtering. I see the applied filters pill details: date, time, and student count. The status banner confirms four labs found, with varying support levels. I am reviewing the first lab card, Lab 04, noting its compatibility, location, computer specs, and installed software. I am seeing the available computers.\n\n\n**Assessing Lab Availability**\n\nI\'m now deeply involved in evaluating lab options from \"Passo 2.\" Lab 04 shows excellent suitability, plus relevant software, and an ideal time window. I\'ve noted Lab 01, which requires software adjustments. Lab Mac 02 is insufficient. I am going to compare and contrast options before reviewing the confirmation stage. Finally, I\'ve noted the bottom sticky bar and the button to advance to \"Revis\303\243o\".\n\n**Confirming Reservation Details**\n\nI have progressed to the final stage, \"Passo 3: Confirma\303\247\303\243o & Comprovante Digital\". The confirmation screen displays the \"Comprovante De Reserva\" header, a back button, and an animated success checkmark.\n\n\n**Verifying Reservation Details**\n\nI have now reached the confirmation screen, and I\'m focused on the \"Comprovante De Reserva\" section. The system confirms my lab allocation approval from the academic department. I\'ve noted the unique protocol snippet `#LR-2023-8941`. The boarding pass details Lab 04 (Bloco B, Sala 204), along with date and software. I also see the access QR code.\n\n\n**Detailing Final Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the final screen details. The confirmation includes \"204 para liberar a entrada 15 min antes.\" and an IT support status card. I\'ve noted the buttons to add to the agenda, share details, and return to the home page.\n\nI am also examining the navigation tabs, including Home, Reserve (a reservation wizard), Labs (a directory of all labs), and History. Furthermore, I am assessing the notifications drawer and profile modal, and software installation request modal. I\'m investigating the Google Font and Icons being used. Finally, I\'m checking the Tailwind configuration.\n\n\n"
