  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Theme Tokens**\n\nOkay, I\'m digging into how Tailwind v4 handles theme tokens. It seems we can leverage either the `@theme` block, custom CSS variables, or a combination of both. I\'ve started examining `Image_2_8047d8e5.html` and the markdown, specifically focusing on the theme colors defined within. So far, the focus is on the  `--color-secondary-fixed`  variable.\n\n\n**Analyzing Color Variables**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out these color variables, like `--color-secondary`, and `--color-on-background`. I\'m starting to understand how they relate to the overall theme. It looks like they contribute to the system\'s design with different surface types, and I\'m looking at their variations now. I\'m focusing on how they\'re intended to be used and in what contexts.\n\n\n**Examining New Tokens**\n\nI\'ve got a fresh batch of tokens to dissect. I\'m noting specific color values like `--color-surface-tint`, `--color-surface-container-low`, and various `--color-primary` and `--color-error` variations. It\'s becoming clearer how these form a consistent visual language, with different surfaces, and how the spacing and font tokens fit in. I\'m looking at how this expands the existing theme.\n\n\n**Integrating Font Definitions**\n\nI\'m now incorporating font definitions into the system. I\'m focusing on the `Plus Jakarta Sans` font and the `Material Symbols Outlined` font, which I need to get from Google Fonts. I\'m also ensuring these are integrated into the `index.html` file. Furthermore, I\'ll review `metadata.json` for proper configuration. Finally, I\'ll check my local assets to ensure everything\'s properly arranged.\n\n\n**Identifying Image Assets**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the image assets being used. I have identified several local files and external URLs, specifically for the logo, avatar, and lab photo banner. I\'m noting the URLs for the image assets to ensure their proper integration, specifically `/public/assets/aistudio/Image_1_952de44c.png`, `/public/assets/aistudio/Image_3_fd8c7b89.png`, `/public/assets/aistudio/Image_5_7441a1b5.png`, and `/public/assets/aistudio/Image_7_6dfb04e6.png`. I\'ll cross-reference these with the HTML to confirm their usage.\n\n\n**Defining App Structure**\n\nI\'m now outlining the application\'s overall structure and its required features, especially considering the user\'s specific request for hotlinked image support. I\'m focusing on the \"In\303\255cio\" screen, determining how to best implement the header elements like the logo, notification bell, and user profile pill, and integrating the welcome greeting and the metric counters. I\'m also considering potential fallback strategies for the hotlinked images.\n\n\n**Planning User Interface**\n\nI\'m now building out the \"In\303\255cio\" screen, focusing on interactive elements. I\'m prioritizing the \"Pr\303\263xima Aula Agendada\" card, which I\'ll render as a spotlight hero. I\'m including key details: time, status (with an emerald badge), subject, lab location, badges for attendees and tools, and a button to view access information. I\'m also adding rapid actions like \"Fazer Nova Reserva,\" \"Consultar Grade de Labs,\" and \"Solicitar Instala\303\247\303\243o de Software.\" Lastly, I\'m integrating a list of upcoming reservations.\n\n\n**Designing Reservation Steps**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \"Nova Reserva\" process, specifically the first step: defining requirements. I\'m building a clear step indicator and an academic context selector, using select boxes for subject and designated class. I\'ve integrated a student count mechanism with decrement, increment, and a slider. The system should provide a dynamic, smart recommendation, based on the student count. Finally, I\'m thinking of a 1:1 student-PC indicator.\n\n\n**Developing Reservation Time**\n\nI\'m now implementing the date and time selection, starting with a dynamic date carousel and the start and end time selections. I\'m building a duration calculator that automatically updates based on these selections, and will show this in a \"Dura\303\247\303\243o\" badge. Next, I\'ll build out the software and environment selectors using multi-select chips. Finally, I\'m working on a dynamic call-to-action button to transition to the next step: lab selection.\n\n\n**Constructing Lab Selections**\n\nI\'m now implementing the lab selection step. I\'ve built a card showing applied filters, and an \"Editar\" button to adjust them. A compatibility banner is being developed, summarizing the results, focusing on labs that are compatible immediately versus those that require adjustments. I\'m creating interactive laboratory cards with details like compatibility, location, computers, software, facilities, availability, and a \"Selecionar este Laborat\303\263rio\" button. I\'ve designed cards for both fully compatible and partially compatible labs, including a \"Solicitar com Instala\303\247\303\243o Pr\303\251via\" button for the latter.\n\n\n**Finalizing Reservation Flow**\n\nI\'m now completing the lab selection. I\'m building detailed lab cards for both compatible and incompatible options. The incompatible option now displays a disabled button \"Indispon\303\255vel para esta turma\". The compatible option indicates the number of computers available. When the user selects a lab, I update the sticky bottom bar with the selected lab\'s name and a call-to-action button, \"Avan\303\247ar para Revis\303\243o\", transitioning to the final confirmation step, which is now being called \"Comprovante de Reserva\".\n\n\n**Designing Ticket Visuals**\n\nI\'m now designing the visual details of the digital pass or ticket card. I\'ve integrated a high-tech lab photo as a header. I\'m focusing on the \"Sala Autenticada\" badge with a pulsing dot, and formatting the details on the card. I\'m outlining the \"Desenvolvimento Web & Mobile\" and professor details, as well as the lab location and capacity. I\'m also including the date, time, and software stack tags. I\'m then implementing a perforated ticket divider, a QR code for access, and a callout for IT support.\n\n\n**Defining Lab Directory**\n\nI\'m now outlining a \"Laborat\303\263rios\" screen with tabs for directory exploration and reservation history. The directory will include an overview of campus labs, status filters, and search capabilities. I\'ll include full specs for each lab, along with a quick reservation button. The history section organizes past, present, and canceled reservations.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Reservation Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on reservation management, creating cards with status indicators like \"Confirmada,\" \"Aguardando TI,\" and \"Conclu\303\255da.\" I\'m implementing a detailed modal to display voucher information, and a cancellation modal with state updates. A \"Download/Print\" option for the voucher is also being added.\n\n\n"
