  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Application Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the application\'s data and component architecture. I\'m starting by identifying the essential components and state models we\'ll need. Right now, I\'m working on defining the `Reservation` type in `types.ts`, which will include fields for things like ID, protocol, subject, professor, and course information, along with classroom and lab details.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structures**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the `Reservation` type with more specific fields. I\'m focusing on incorporating details like `studentsCount`, `dateStr`, `dayOfWeek`, and IT ticket information. I\'m also planning to create mock database and localStorage data in `src/data/mockData.ts`, starting with some initial `Lab` entries.\n\n\n**Cataloging Lab Resources**\n\nI\'m now cataloging our lab resources meticulously. I have detailed information on five labs: Sala 204, Lab 01, Lab Mac 02, Lab 05, and Lab 03, including specific locations, hardware specs (CPU, RAM, storage), software availability (like Android Studio, VS Code, Python, and more), and additional features (like projectors, air conditioning, and backup power). This will inform the component details.\n\n\n**Detailing Hardware & Software**\n\nI\'ve been gathering hardware and software specifics for each lab, focusing on five labs (Sala 204, Lab 01, Lab Mac 02, Lab 05, and Lab 03). The information encompasses CPU, RAM, storage, and software like AutoCAD, Revit, SolidWorks, MATLAB, and Blender for one. I\'m also now compiling initial reservation data and a pre-populated software list to inform the user interface.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Designing Component Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focused on the component structure, specifically starting with a modular design. I am going to have a fixed `Header.tsx` at the top with the LabReserve logo, subtitle options, and a notifications trigger with an unread badge counter.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI component architecture. I have a plan for `Header.tsx` at the top with the lab reserve logo, subtitle, notifications trigger, and user profile. Also, `BottomNav.tsx` will have a fixed bottom tab bar. I am now working on `HomeScreen.tsx` to match the given design. I am also working on `ReservationWizard.tsx` to handle Step 1 (Requisitos), Step 2 (Escolha da Sala) and leading to Step 3.\n\n\n**Mapping UI Steps**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user interface flow for the reservation process, specifically the second step. I\'m focusing on the \"Escolha da Sala\" section, which includes an active stepper indication. I\'m structuring a filtered results bar with an \"Editar\" button to return to the previous step. Additionally, I\'m defining compatibility summary cards with green badges and detailed lab cards for each available option, including software, specs, and facilities. I am building the lab cards with a \"Selecionar este Laborat\303\263rio\" button. I am also planning for adjustment of software necessity with installation notifications.\n\n\n**Finalizing Reservation Details**\n\nI\'m now implementing the final reservation confirmation view. I\'m focusing on the voucher details, ensuring it matches the specified design including a success checkmark, protocol snippet, and a boarding pass-style ticket. The ticket will include all reservation details: subject, professor, lab information, date, duration, software list, and a digital QR code for access. I\'m also adding buttons for calendar integration and sharing the confirmation.\n\n\n**Structuring Application Navigation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on navigation components and screen design. I\'m building `LabsDirectoryScreen.tsx` for viewing labs with filters and hardware search, `HistoryScreen.tsx` for reservation history, `QrAccessModal.tsx` for digital door access, and `SoftwareRequestModal.tsx` for software requests. I\'m also preparing `NotificationsDrawer.tsx` and `ProfileModal.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_36126"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export interface Lab {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  category: string;\\n  block: string;\\n  floor: string;\\n  roomNumber: string;\\n  totalComputers: number;\\n  cpu: string;\\n  ram: string;\\n  storage: string;\\n  gpu?: string;\\n  installedSoftware: string[];\\n  airConditioned: boolean;\\n  projector: string;\\n  whiteBoard: boolean;\\n  noBreak: boolean;\\n  availableHours: string;\\n  isIdealWindow: boolean;\\n  status: \'disponivel\' | \'manutencao\' | \'ocupado\';\\n  image?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Reservation {\\n  id: string;\\n  protocol: string;\\n  subject: string;\\n  course: string;\\n  assignedClass: string;\\n  professorName: string;\\n  siape: string;\\n  labId: string;\\n  labName: string;\\n  location: string;\\n  studentsCount: number;\\n  totalStations: number;\\n  dateStr: string;\\n  dateFormatted: string;\\n  startTime: string;\\n  endTime: string;\\n  durationStr: string;\\n  requiredSoftware: string[];\\n  extraSoftware?: string;\\n  status: \'confirmada\' | \'aguardando_ti\' | \'concluida\' | \'cancelada\';\\n  requiresItSupport?: boolean;\\n  itTicket?: {\\n    id: string;\\n    description: string;\\n    estimatedTime: string;\\n    status: \'em_andamento\' | \'concluido\' | \'pendente\';\\n  };\\n  qrCodeText: string;\\n  createdAt: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SoftwareCategory {\\n  id: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  items: string[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface NotificationItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  timestamp: string;\\n  read: boolean;\\n  type: \'info\' | \'success\' | \'warning\' | \'alert\';\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Define core TypeScript interfaces for LabReserve\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating types.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create types.ts\"}"
