  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Requirements**\n\nI\'m deep in the new user requirements. Desktop responsiveness is my current focus. I\'m making sure this application will be beautiful and fully functional on desktops too, and not limited to just a mobile frame.\n\n\n**Defining Access Control**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to access control and the professor/administrator roles. I\'m exploring seamless role switching for testing, maybe a profile switcher. This will be key to understanding the differing workflows. I\'m specifically thinking about how to allow an easy way to test both roles.\n\n\n**Clarifying Lab Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of lab management. I\'m nailing down the CRUD operations for rooms and their associated properties like naming conventions (Bloco + N\303\272mero), software lists, and capacity.  Also, I\'m integrating room status (reserved/free) with date and time schedules to make the labs management more useful to users.\n\n\n**Implementing Image Sharing**\n\nI\'m now focused on enabling professors to share lab schedules visually. I\'ve landed on generating high-resolution `.jpg` image cards directly from a `<canvas>` element using `canvas.toDataURL`. It\'s a clean solution with no external dependencies and works well with the existing infrastructure. I\'m checking the current file structure (e.g., `src/types.ts`, `src/data/mockData.ts`, various components). My Skill Check also confirms this aligns with the universal design principles.\n\n\n**Defining Room Naming**\n\nI\'m now designing the lab\'s data model. The room naming convention will be `Bloco` + `N\303\272mero`, prominently displayed and used internally. I\'m focusing on the data structure, with fields for `code` (e.g., `B204`), `name` (e.g., \"B204 - Dev Lab\"), `block`, `floor`, and `roomNumber`. The `Lab` interface will also include capacity, software, hardware, and status with optional schedules.\n\n\n**Structuring Reservation Data**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining reservation data. I\'m building out the `Reservation` interface, adding fields such as `protocol`, `subject`, `assignedClass`, `professorName`, student count,  required software, and reservation status. I\'m focusing on the relationship between reservation, labs, and schedules, including fields for reservation status (`pendente`, `aprovada`, etc.) and lab assignment (lab ID, code, and name) which are important administrative aspects. I\'m carefully considering how to represent reservation times and dates.\n\n\n**Refining Reservation Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating new reservation attributes. I\'m adding `assignedLocation`, `adminJustification`, `reviewedAt`, and `reviewedBy` to the reservation interface, all as strings. Also, the fields `qrCodeText` and `createdAt` will be added. This also includes the user role definition, including professor and admin with clear role distinctions for testing. I\'m focusing on a smooth role switcher in the header and profile modal for quick toggle between professor and admin views with a visual badge.\nI am also working on the Professor\'s flow for requesting a room, where only class requirements will be needed: subject, class designation, student count, date, start and end times, and required software.\n\n\n**Finalizing Request Flow**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the professor\'s room request and notification system. The professor submits the request, and its status immediately updates to \'pending\'. Upon approval, the professor is notified and can view the assigned room details, including the generated digital voucher and QR code for the door. They can then share or download the `.jpg` card, which I\'m designing with a 16:9 or Instagram ratio, and features key information: room code, discipline, and professor name.\n\n\n\n**Designing Image Output**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the image generation for room reservations. I\'m adding a \"Direct Download\" button for the `.jpg` image and implementing a \"Web Share API\" button with a fallback for browser compatibility. The image will include data such as date and time, room capacity, authorized software, and an institutional stamp. The download is named `card-reserva-B204.jpg`.\n\nI\'m also considering the Administrator features to manage requests. They\'ll have a section for \"Pending Requests,\" showing details like subject, professor, student count, and software. The system will suggest suitable rooms, and admins can accept, assign a room, and notify the professor. Rejection will require an explanation.\n\n\n**Implementing Room CRUD**\n\nI\'m now implementing the lab room management system. I\'m focusing on the CRUD operations: listing rooms with filtering by block, status, and software. I\'m also working on detailed room views using the standard room code format. I\'ve designed the forms to create, edit, and delete rooms, allowing the specification of room details such as code, block, floor, software, capacity, and status. I\'m also making sure the admin can view room schedules to check availabilities. The desktop view is being adapted with an expanded interface.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_74313"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export type UserRole = \'professor\' | \'admin\';\\n\\nexport interface ScheduleSlot {\\n  id: string;\\n  date: string; // YYYY-MM-DD\\n  startTime: string; // HH:mm\\n  endTime: string; // HH:mm\\n  reservationId: string;\\n  subject: string;\\n  professorName: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Lab {\\n  id: string;\\n  code: string; // e.g. \\\"B204\\\", \\\"C302\\\", \\\"A102\\\" - Standard Bloco + N\303\272mero\\n  name: string; // e.g. \\\"B204 - Laborat\303\263rio de Desenvolvimento\\\"\\n  category: string;\\n  block: string; // \\\"Bloco B\\\"\\n  floor: string; // \\\"2\302\272 Andar\\\"\\n  roomNumber: string; // \\\"204\\\"\\n  capacity: number; // Tamanho da sala (computadores)\\n  cpu: string;\\n  ram: string;\\n  storage: string;\\n  gpu?: string;\\n  installedSoftware: string[];\\n  airConditioned: boolean;\\n  projector: string;\\n  whiteBoard: boolean;\\n  noBreak: boolean;\\n  availableHours: string;\\n  status: \'livre\' | \'reservada\' | \'manutencao\';\\n  scheduleSlots?: ScheduleSlot[];\\n  image?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport type ReservationStatus = \'pendente\' | \'confirmada\' | \'rejeitada\' | \'aguardando_ti\' | \'concluida\';\\n\\nexport interface Reservation {\\n  id: string;\\n  protocol: string; // e.g. \\\"#LR-2023-8941\\\"\\n  subject: string;\\n  course: string;\\n  assignedClass: string;\\n  professorName: string;\\n  professorId: string;\\n  siape: string;\\n\\n  // Class specs requested by professor\\n  studentsCount: number;\\n  dateStr: string; // YYYY-MM-DD\\n  dateFormatted: string;\\n  startTime: string; // HH:mm\\n  endTime: string; // HH:mm\\n  durationStr: string;\\n  requiredSoftware: string[];\\n  extraSoftware?: string;\\n\\n  // Administrative Allocation\\n  status: ReservationStatus;\\n  assignedLabId?: string;\\n  assignedLabCode?: string; // e.g. \\\"B204\\\", \\\"C302\\\"\\n  assignedLabName?: string;\\n  assignedLocation?: string; // \\\"Bloco B, Sala 204\\\"\\n  totalStations?: number;\\n\\n  adminJustification?: string; // Rejection justification or admin notes\\n  reviewedAt?: string;\\n  reviewedBy?: string;\\n\\n  requiresItSupport?: boolean;\\n  itTicket?: {\\n    id: string;\\n    description: string;\\n    estimatedTime: string;\\n    status: \'em_andamento\' | \'concluido\' | \'pendente\';\\n  };\\n  qrCodeText: string;\\n  createdAt: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SoftwareCategory {\\n  id: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  items: string[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface NotificationItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  timestamp: string;\\n  read: boolean;\\n  type: \'info\' | \'success\' | \'warning\' | \'alert\' | \'error\';\\n  targetRole?: UserRole; // \'professor\' or \'admin\'\\n  reservationId?: string;\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Update TypeScript interfaces with UserRole, ScheduleSlot, room code standard, and administrative review fields\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating types.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update types.ts\"}"
